### DINE (Durham Intelligent NIC Environment)

Log into the first DINE node as by documentation (`ssh -X b101`).

##### Configuration with Intel MPI and OneAPI

For some applications (such as CCZ4), you will need additional packages
(`module load gsl/2.5` for example). Old MPI implementations seem to
struggle with single sided communication. In this case, you have to add
`-DnoMPISupportsSingleSidedCommunication` to the `CXXFLAGS`. With the
module combination from above, the single-sided communication flag seems
not to be necessary anymore.

The current MPI installation of DINE seems to face issues when we assign
cores to MPI ranks: Often, only two cores are assigned to the first
rank, while the other ranks get only one core. In this case, you have to
tell `mpirun` explicitly that it has to use multiple cores per rank:

mpirun -n myNoOfRank -cpus-per-rank CoresPerRank ./peano4 \...

