### Bede

Access to Bede can be requested through SAFE
(<https://safe.epcc.ed.ac.uk/>). The machine then is reachable through
`ssh` with `ssh <username>@bede.dur.ac.uk`

##### Prepare the Python and bash environment

You will need to run this commmand once to obtain a proper compile
environment:

Then log out and log in again.

To install Python with all packages, run

python3 -m venv $HOME/peano-python-api
source$HOME/peano-python-api/bin/activate pip install jinja2 sympy

##### Build with LLVM and MVAPICH

LLVM is the recommended compiler for  on Bede. OpenMPI initially has
been more robust on Bede, but the installation struggles with
single-sided MPI. We therefore prefer newer versions of mvapich:

module load nsight-systems cuda llvm module load mvapich2/2.3.5-2
./configure --enable-exahype --enable-loadbalancing-toolbox
 --with-multithreading=omp --with-mpi=mpicxx  CXX=clang++

The GPU support is added via

module load nsight-systems cuda llvm module load mvapich2/2.3.5-2
./configure --enable-exahype --enable-loadbalancing-toolbox
 --with-multithreading=omp --with-mpi=mpicxx --with-gpu=omp  CXX=clang++
 CXXFLAGS=\"-fopenmp -fopenmp-targets=nvptx64-nvidia-cuda\"

##### Build with LLVM and OpenMPI

OpenMPI initially has been more robust on Bede, but the installation
struggles with single-sided MPI. We therefore prefer newer versions of
mvapich (see above). If you insist on OpenMPI, you have switch off the
non-critical assertions:

module load nsight-systems cuda llvm module load openmpi ./configure
\... CXXFLAGS=\" \... -DnoMPISupportsSingleSidedCommunication\"
*/